From e3d471fc3be18cb9081cc0a2b11bca61cb30119e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:19:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 49/51] drm/gma500: share the SGX545 TA/3D job builders with
 the render node

Split sgx_tri.c in two. The new sgx_render.c builds the kernel-owned side of
a TA + 3D job: the HW render context, the parameter buffer descriptor,
block and page table, the RT data set, and for each scene the render
details, the TA command and the background object. It takes the scene's
register words as a struct drm_sgxfive_render_cmd and the addresses of the
context's structures, so the render node can build its jobs with it.
sgx_tri.c keeps what a client builds: the first triangle's programs, MTE
state, VDM stream and geometry, and now also its register words.

The debugfs triangle tests build their job through the new path. The KUnit
tests move with the code and keep the exact values the laptop ran; a new
case checks that the background object built from the register words is
the one the transfer builder made from the program addresses
(sgx_xfer_bgobj_words, factored out of sgx_xfer_bgobj). On the laptop the
triangle renders as before, in both kick forms and page directories.

Assisted-by: LLM
